.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt SYSADMINCTL 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysadminctl
.Nd manage user accounts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl addUser Ar name
.Op Fl fullName Ar full_name
.Op Fl UID Ar uid
.Op Fl shell Ar path
.Op Fl password Ar password | Fl
.Op Fl home Ar path
.Op Fl admin
.Nm
.Fl deleteUser Ar name
.Op Fl secure | Fl keepHome
.Nm
.Fl resetPasswordFor Ar name
.Fl newPassword Ar password | Fl
.Nm
.Fl secureTokenStatus Ar name
.Nm
.Fl guestAccount Cm status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates, deletes and changes the local user accounts, kept in
.Pa /etc/master.passwd
(the databases are rebuilt with
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8 )
and
.Pa /etc/group .
It must be run as root.
It reports what it does on the standard error, each line stamped with the
time and the process.
A password given as
.Fl
is asked for on the terminal.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl addUser Ar name
Create the account: the first free user ID from 501 unless
.Fl UID
gives one, the
.Li staff
group, the full name (the name itself unless
.Fl fullName ) ,
the home
.Pa /Users/ Ns Ar name
(or
.Fl home )
with the folders Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Library, Movies, Music,
Pictures and Public, and
.Pa /bin/zsh
(or
.Fl shell ) .
The password is stored as a SHA-512
.Xr crypt 3
hash; without
.Fl password
the account is created locked.
.Fl admin
adds the user to the
.Li admin
group.
.It Fl deleteUser Ar name
End the user's processes, delete the account, take the user out of every
group and remove the home under
.Pa /Users ,
unless
.Fl keepHome .
.Fl secure
is accepted.
System accounts (user IDs below 501) are not deleted.
.It Fl resetPasswordFor Ar name Fl newPassword Ar password
Set the user's password.
.It Fl secureTokenStatus Ar name
Disabled: there is no volume encryption yet.
.It Fl guestAccount Cm status
Whether a Guest account exists.
.El
.Pp
.Fl hint ,
.Fl passwordHint ,
.Fl picture ,
.Fl adminUser
and
.Fl adminPassword
are accepted and not used.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
.It Pa /etc/group
.It Pa /Users
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chpass 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8 ,
.Xr vipw 8
